	(text "the pn532 is a intresting looking module\n which will definitely catch attention so im using this, \nhowever you can use other moduel without a problem.\nthe module has 8 pins so we are making 8 pin connecter\n in which we will put our module either by solder the module \npins direct or connect those pin connector there are in \narduino but that may make my design thicker which is \nsomething i dont want"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 123.19 105.41 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.016 1.016)
			)
		)
		(uuid "12c5c6dc-f1d5-477e-81b9-c332da71dafe")
	)
	(text "ST7735 VCC  → Pico 3V3\nST7735 GND  → Pico GND\n\nST7735 SCL  → GP18\nST7735 SDA  → GP19\n\nST7735 CS   → GP20\nST7735 DC   → GP21\nST7735 RES  → GP22\n\nST7735 BLK  → Pico 3V3"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 134.62 34.29 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "37578946-570d-4124-b4f9-3eef435c2bd3")
	)
	(text "i orginally planned to use the seed studio rp2040 xiao \nbecause its compact and i have one laying around.\nbut after i started laying my pins out i realised\n i would have to share pins or like do some weird \nstuff to get it to work.\ni was also going to use my own devboard that ive made based on the rp2040. \nthe raspberry pico has a onboard regulator so i wont have to use the ME6211C33M5."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 58.42 115.57 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.016 1.016)
			)
		)
		(uuid "68d7923c-aa4d-420b-982c-deac87db3dbb")
